# Prettier owns source. It does not own files that something other than a human
# editing them wrote — formatting those either flip-flops on the next write or
# edits a record. Keep this list short: everything else, including every JSON
# file under `src/`, is prettier's.

# pnpm rewrites the lockfile in its own format on every install, so a
# prettier-formatted lockfile survives exactly until the next `pnpm install`.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Drift measurements captured from a live browser session, at the indent the
# capture produced. They are evidence, and they sit beside the PNGs in that
# folder as the same class of artefact — nothing imports them, so the only
# effect of formatting them is to edit the record. The next dump pasted in
# would reintroduce the diff anyway.
docs/globe/*.json
